  "helpTitle": "Help",
  "helpContent": "Start here to learn CharmShelf one step at a time. You can read only the part you need.\n\n## 1. Add a file\n1. Open Library and tap +.\n2. Choose Add a file or Add a folder.\n3. Choose the file on your device, then tap Add.\n4. A single imported file opens automatically when it finishes. For multiple files or folders, open the contents from the results screen.\n\n> Adding a file creates a copy inside the app. The original is not moved or deleted. The copy needs free space on your device.\n\n## 2. Keep a catalog together\nA catalog treats files as one unit.\nA folder you add starts as one catalog, with photos to enjoy like a photo book or music like an album.\nA single file can be a catalog too, with charms, a cover, and favorites of its own.\nYou can change this with Change grouping just before you add.\n\n## 3. Add a charm\nA charm is your own marker, such as Travel or Recipes. Add several to one catalog to make it yours and find it again by those markers.\nAdd one from the file or catalog menu. You can still find an item by its name without a charm.\n\n## 4. Find something\nSearch from the magnifying glass in Library. It looks through the whole library by name and charm.\nIf something is missing, clear the search words and filters.\nHome shows what you opened recently and your favorites.\n\n## 5. Keep your data safe\nKeep original files outside the app as well. Removing the app deletes its copies, charms, notes, and favorites.\nIn Settings, Library Backup saves and restores app-managed files together with charms, aliases, notes, favorites, and viewing history. Restoration adds a dedicated folder and preserves existing data with the same identity. Copy legacy external references into the library first. Backups include hidden, archived, and trashed content. Backup files are not encrypted. Check their contents and destination and store them securely. App-lock passcodes, biometric settings, and OS access permissions are excluded.\nExporting only charm definitions does not back up assignments, favorites, or notes.\nHiding an item only removes it from the list. It does not lock the file. If other people can open your device, turn on App Lock in Settings first. A forgotten passcode cannot be recovered in this app.\n\n## 6. If something goes wrong\n- **Worried about deleting something?** After you move an item to the trash, you can restore it until you empty the trash. Read the confirmation.\n- **Cannot find a file?** Clear search and filters.\n- **Display looks wrong?** Restart the app and check free device storage.\n- **Using a shared device?** Use a device lock and App Lock in Settings. Hiding an item is not protection.\n\nContact: [Send an email](mailto:deeple+charmshelfstaff@inkboxmail.com)",
  "termsOfServiceTitle": "Terms of Service",
  "termsOfServiceContent": "Last updated: 2026-11-02\n\nThese Terms set out the conditions for using CharmShelf (the \"App\"), provided by the Developer.\n\n**At a glance**\n- The App handles files and organization data on your device. Keep separate copies of important originals.\n- Support for the Developer is an optional one-time purchase. It does not unlock features or renew.\n- The App and bundled software are subject to their respective licenses. See \"Licenses\" for details.\n\n## 1. Scope and Agreement\n- These Terms set out conditions for the use, support, and developer support purchases offered by the Developer for the App.\n- By downloading, installing, or using the App, you are deemed to agree to these Terms only within their applicable scope.\n- These Terms do not impose additional restrictions on rights to use, copy, modify, redistribute, or otherwise exercise permissions granted for software or assets under the MIT License or other open-source licenses. If these Terms conflict with a license, the license applicable to the relevant software or asset takes precedence.\n\n## 2. Eligibility and Minors\n- If a minor uses the App, they must obtain the prior consent of a legal representative (parent or guardian).\n- If a minor uses the App without legal representative consent and continues to use the App after reaching the age of majority, they are deemed to have ratified their past actions during their minority.\n\n## 3. User Responsibilities and Data Management\n- Users shall use the App at their own responsibility and expense, properly maintaining their device, OS, and network environment.\n- Users bear full responsibility for rights clearance and legal compliance regarding files (images, videos, documents, etc.) managed, referenced, or displayed in the App.\n- The App provides user-initiated library backup and restoration to a destination you select. Backups are not encrypted and include hidden, archived, and trashed content; store them securely. Copy legacy external references into the library first. Restoration adds a dedicated folder and preserves existing data with the same identity. Exporting only charm definitions does not back up the library. Keep important originals separately as well.\n\n## 4. Developer Support Purchases\n- Tips are one-time consumable purchases. They do not unlock features or renew automatically, and the same product may be purchased more than once.\n- Check the price retrieved from the store in the App and confirm the amount in the store purchase sheet.\n- Consumed tips cannot be restored. Unfinished transactions are retried using the store's transaction information.\n- Payments, purchase history, and refund requests are handled through the App Store or Google Play. Refund eligibility is governed by applicable law and the relevant store's decision.\n\n## 5. Intellectual Property\n- Intellectual property rights in programs, designs, trademarks, and logos comprising the App belong to the Developer or rightful third-party licensors.\n- The App code is licensed under MIT. Bundled third-party software and assets are governed by their respective licenses. See \"Licenses\" in the App for details.\n\n## 6. Prohibited Acts\nUsers shall not engage in any of the following:\n- Acts violating laws, court orders, or public order and morals\n- Acts related to criminal activity or providing benefits to anti-social forces\n- Infringing intellectual property, privacy, reputation, or other rights of the Developer or third parties\n- Handling unlawful material (child pornography, uncensored obscene material, etc.) prohibited by law\n- Unauthorized access to systems without permission, or exploiting vulnerabilities in a way that infringes others' rights\n\n## 7. Changes to the App\n- The Developer may add, modify, or terminate all or part of the App without prior notice.\n- The Developer may temporarily suspend the App for maintenance, natural disasters, network failures, or other unavoidable reasons.\n\n## 8. Disclaimer and Limitation of Liability\n- The Developer does not guarantee that the App is free from defects (including defects in safety, reliability, accuracy, completeness, fitness for purpose, bugs, or non-infringement).\n- Device failure, OS changes, storage problems, app removal, and mistakes may cause files or organization data to be lost or become inaccessible.\n- The Developer’s liability is governed by the Consumer Contract Act and other applicable law. These Terms do not exclude liability that cannot be excluded by law.\n\n## 9. Changes to Terms\n- The Developer may amend these Terms in accordance with Article 548-4 of the Civil Code of Japan (Standard Terms and Conditions) or relevant regulations.\n- Amendments, effective dates, and modified terms will be announced within the App or via other appropriate channels.\n\n## 10. Anti-Social Forces\nUsers represent and warrant that they do not belong to anti-social forces (organized crime groups, etc.) and will not engage in violent or unlawful demands.\n\n## 11. Governing Law and Jurisdiction\n- These Terms are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of Japan.\n- Any disputes related to the App shall be submitted to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Tokyo District Court in the first instance.\n\n## 12. Language\nThe Japanese version of these Terms is the official and controlling version. Any translated version is provided for reference only, and the Japanese version prevails in case of conflict.\n\n## 13. Contact\nCharmShelf Development Team: [deeple+charmshelfstaff@inkboxmail.com](mailto:deeple+charmshelfstaff@inkboxmail.com)",
  "privacyPolicyTitle": "Privacy Policy",
  "privacyPolicyContent": "Last updated: 2026-09-01\n\n## 1. Basic Policy & Operator Information\nCharmShelf (the \"App\") is committed to protecting your privacy. We adopt a \"local-first architecture\" where your library data and personal files are processed and stored primarily on your local device.\n\n- Operator: Private Shelf Project (CharmShelf Development Team)\n- Contact: [deeple+charmshelfstaff@inkboxmail.com](mailto:deeple+charmshelfstaff@inkboxmail.com)\n\n## 2. Information Stored on Your Device\nTo provide its features, the App handles the following data primarily on your device. When you choose to share, export, or send information for support, the selected data is provided to the recipient or service you choose. None of this data is automatically transmitted to external servers:\n- Media & File Data: Files imported into the App or referenced with your permission (photos, videos, audio, PDFs, text, etc.)\n- Library Management Information: Folder structures, charms, aliases, notes, favorites, sort orders, and hidden/archive states\n- Import Sources & Migration Data: Device file listings are used temporarily to select import sources. Previously saved source candidates, labels and external-reference migration records are kept on-device for migration and recovery. Originals are not modified.\n- App Settings & Cache: Display preferences, thumbnail images, and performance cache\n- Local Crash Logs: Error logs generated temporarily on-device for troubleshooting\n\n## 3. Zero-Tracking & No External Transmission\n- Zero Third-Party Tracking: The App does not integrate any third-party advertising SDKs or behavioral analytics SDKs (such as Google Analytics, Firebase, or Facebook SDK). We never track your activity or collect advertising identifiers (IDFA/AAID).\n- No Automatic External Transmission: Unless explicitly initiated by you (e.g., sending support emails, using the system share sheet), your files and personal data are never sent to external servers.\n- Automatic backup exclusion: App-managed private storage is configured to be excluded from automatic cloud backup and device-to-device transfer. Shared or exported data, information sent to support, external originals, and copies held by external services are outside this exclusion.\n\n## 4. Purpose of Permissions Used\nThe App requests permissions strictly for legitimate core functionalities:\n- Storage / File Access Permissions (Android: All Files Access / iOS: Document Storage): Used to select and preview import sources, copy files into the library, export and restore files you authorize the App to access.\n- Camera & Photos Library: Used to take photos/videos directly into your library or select and export files.\n- Biometric Authentication (Face ID / Touch ID / Fingerprint): Used for unlocking the app lock and re-authentication. Biometric data is processed entirely within the device's secure hardware (Secure Enclave / Keystore) and is never accessed or stored by the App.\n- Notifications: Used to show file import progress and completion. Imports remain available without notification permission.\n- Network State Check: Used solely to verify connectivity when opening external help/legal web pages and to manage offline status.\n\n## 5. Limits of Protection & Disclaimers\n- Hidden & Archive States: These features organize and restrict visibility within the App UI; they do not irreversibly encrypt files on the filesystem.\n- App Lock: Restricts unauthorized access to the App screen, but does not prevent direct physical access to the device or filesystem-level access via OS tools.\n- Backup and data protection: In Settings, Library Backup saves and restores app-managed files together with charms, aliases, notes, favorites, and viewing history. Restoration adds a dedicated folder and preserves existing data with the same identity. Copy legacy external references into the library first. Backups include hidden, archived, and trashed content. Backup files are not encrypted. Check their contents and destination and store them securely. App-lock passcodes, biometric settings, and OS access permissions are excluded. Keep important original files outside the app as well.\n- Disclaimer: The developer is not liable for data loss or leakage caused by device loss, hardware failure, OS updates, user errors, or forgotten passwords. Keep separate copies of important originals outside the app and verify that you can open them at their destination.\n\n## 6. External Data Sharing\nWhen you perform the following actions, data is transferred to the destination you select and is subject to that destination's policies:\n- Sharing files via the OS Share Sheet to other apps, cloud services, or messaging tools\n- Exporting selected files to external storage or cloud services\n- Sending diagnostic or support inquiries to the developer via email\n\n## 7. Retention & Deletion\n- In-app deletion affects the items identified in the confirmation screen. Private app storage on Android and iOS is normally removed on uninstall, including management information saved within the app.\n- Removing a previous external reference removes its registration and related metadata while leaving the original file in place. Private migration snapshots and staged copies are retained for recovery.\n- Android public recovery folders, external source files, shared destinations, and exported files may remain after uninstall. Charms and catalog settings are not automatically restored from original files.\n\n## 8. Minor & Children Privacy (COPPA / GDPR Compliance)\nThe App is suitable for all ages and never knowingly or intentionally collects personal data from children under 13 or minors. Minors should obtain guardian consent when required.\n\n## 9. Policy Updates\nThis Policy may be updated to reflect feature improvements or legal changes. Updates take effect once posted within the App or on the official page.\n\n## 10. Contact Us\nFor privacy inquiries, please contact:\n- CharmShelf Development Team\n- Email: [deeple+charmshelfstaff@inkboxmail.com](mailto:deeple+charmshelfstaff@inkboxmail.com)",
